## 4. SOURCE CODE DISCLOSURE (MODIFIED SERVERS)

If you run or distribute a Server using a Modified Version of the Software, you must make the complete corresponding source code publicly available.

This includes:
- All modifications to the Software
- Any additional code required to run the Server that interacts with the Software logic
- Build scripts or configuration required to reproduce the running version (excluding secrets like passwords or API keys)

The source code must be:
- Freely accessible
- Without payment
- Without login or access restriction

